    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "Sometimes the people behind it get caught. In August twenty twenty three, police in Cyprus arrested a man named Arthur Petrov at America's request. Prosecutors said he used a shell company to buy American microelectronics, claimed they were headed somewhere else, and shipped them to suppliers of the Russian military. A month later, another man, Maxim Marchenko, was arrested and charged with using shell companies in Hong Kong to send American-made military-grade displays to Russia, the kind used in rifle scopes and night vision gear. For every case that reaches a courtroom, investigators believe many more never do.",
